=== PE 843: Periodic Circles ===

=== Ford Circles Properties ===
The Ford circles form a periodic pattern over [0,1]
that repeats with period 1.

Ford circles with q ≤ N:
  N=10: areas sum = 0.8700146712, perimeters sum = 6.6344179779
  N=30: areas sum = 0.8720226440, perimeters sum = 8.7011770288
  N=100: areas sum = 0.8722601961, perimeters sum = 10.9873761191

=== Circle Packings in a Periodic Domain ===
Consider circles on a 2D torus or periodic strip.
Periodic circle arrangements often relate to:
  - Farey sequences (Ford circles)
  - Modular forms and hyperbolic geometry
  - Apollonian gasket with periodic boundary

